.TH OMX\-CLAP\-SCAN 1 "October 2026" "omx-clap-host @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx\-clap\-scan \- list the plugins, parameters and ports of CLAP plugin files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx\-clap\-scan
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RI [ path ...]
.br
.B omx\-clap\-scan \-\-fields
.BI clap: path # id
|
.BI lv2: uri
|
.B \-\-list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B omx\-clap\-scan
loads each
.I path
(a
.B .clap
file, or a directory searched recursively for
.B .clap
files, in name order) and lists every plugin of its factory: id, name, vendor,
version, description, url and features, then, from an initialised instance
that is destroyed again and never activated, every parameter (id, name,
module, min, max, default, flags by name), the audio ports (main or aux,
channels, kind, a surround port's map or an ambisonic port's ordering and
normalisation, the name, and, for a plugin the core admits as omx\-clap\-host
opens it, the JACK ports that host registers for it:
.BI in_ k\fR,
.BI out_ k\fR,
.BI aux_in_ p _ k
and
.BI aux_out_ p _ k\fR),
the note port counts and the latency.
.PP
The latency is left out when the plugin reports 0 before it is activated,
since that answer is not a measurement.
.PP
With no
.I path
the search path is
.BR CLAP_PATH ,
then
.IR ~/.clap ,
.I /usr/lib64/clap
and
.IR /usr/lib/clap .
.PP
Each file is scanned in a child process. A file that can't be loaded, a
plugin that fails to initialise, a crash or a scan longer than 30 seconds is
reported for that file or plugin, and the scan goes on.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
One JSON document on stdout, keys in a fixed order:
.B scanner, version, files
with, per file,
.B path
and either
.B plugins
or
.BR error .
Without it the same facts are printed as a listing for a person.
.TP
.BI \-\-fields " target"
The field dump of one plugin, what plugin\-hostd's format tables read: the line
.B # omx\-clap\-scan \-\-fields 1
then one record a line,
.IR scope " TAB " field " TAB " value .
A scope is
.BR plugin ,
.BI param: i\fR,
.BI audio_in: i\fR,
.BI audio_out: i\fR,
.BI note_in: i\fR,
.BI note_out: i
(CLAP) or
.BI port: i
(LV2, by lv2:index); a field is a CLAP struct member
.RB ( clap_param_info.min_value )
or an LV2 predicate as a CURIE
.RB ( lv2:minimum );
a number is written %.17g, a CLAP constant by its name, one record per flag set, an LV2 URI as a CURIE.
.BI clap: path # id
is read through an instance of the plugin, created, initialised and activated once at 48 kHz when it offers
clap.latency or clap.voice\-info;
.BI lv2: uri
is found on
.B LV2_PATH
and read through the LV2 adapter's lilv world: its binary is never opened. The dump is written only when whole;
what the plugin prints goes to stderr.
.B \-\-list
writes every name the dump spells a CLAP value by, every LV2 field it asks and every prefix it writes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when at least one path could be read, even if some plugins reported errors;
1 when no path could be read; 2 on a bad option.
With
.BR \-\-fields :
0 the dump is written; 1 the plugin could not be read, and nothing is written; 2 on a bad target.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omx\-clap\-host (1)
